[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a quick-start “sandbox” you can drop into any project that already uses **MapLibre GL JS**.  
It shows you how to point the map at a **public, no-key tile service** (or a tiny local PMTiles file) so you can verify that the rest of your code works before you start wiring up your own tiles or a paid provider.

---

## 1️⃣ Pick a free, key-less tile source

| What you get | URL you can use in a MapLibre style | Notes |
|--------------|-------------------------------------|-------|
| **MapLibre demo style (vector tiles + sprites + glyphs)** | `https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json` | The official “hello-world” style that ships with every MapLibre release. No token, works everywhere. |
| **OpenFreeMap (vector tiles, open-source style)** | `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty` | Community-funded, OSM-based vector tiles. No API key required. |
| **OpenStreetMap raster tiles** (good for quick tests, not vector) | `https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png` | Use a *raster* source in your style if you only need a basemap. |
| **PMTiles (single-file, offline)** | `https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/pmtiles@latest/dist/PMTiles.js` + a `.pmtiles` file | Great for local testing or CI – no network request after the file is loaded. |
| **MapTiler “basic” style (free tier, no key for the demo style)** | `https://api.maptiler.com/maps/basic/style.json?key=YOUR_KEY` | Requires a key, but the free tier is generous. Mentioned here for completeness. |

> **The safest “plug-and-play” choice is the first one – the MapLibre demo style.** It uses the same vector-tile format (`.pbf`) that Mapbox styles use, so you can keep the rest of your code unchanged.

---

## 2️⃣ Minimal MapLibre setup that works with any of the URLs above

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – no-key test</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=1,user-scalable=no" />
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  // 1️⃣ Import the ES-module build (v6+ ships ES-modules only)
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  // 2️⃣ Choose the style you want to test
  const styleUrl = 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json';   // ← change this line
  // const styleUrl = 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty';
  // const styleUrl = 'https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'; // raster example (see below)

  // 3️⃣ Create the map
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: styleUrl,
    center: [-122.42, 37.78], // San Francisco
    zoom: 12
  });

  // 4️⃣ Add a few handy controls (optional)
  map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl());
  map.addControl(new maplibregl.ScaleControl({ maxWidth: 80, unit: 'metric' }));
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What to change

| Situation | What to edit |
|-----------|--------------|
| **Use the OpenFreeMap vector style** | `const styleUrl = 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty';` |
| **Use a raster OSM basemap** (no vector tiles) | Replace the `style` property with a *style object* that defines a raster source, e.g.:<br><br>`style: { version: 8, sources: { osm: { type: 'raster', tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'], tileSize: 256 } }, layers: [{ id: 'osm', type: 'raster', source: 'osm' }] }` |
| **Load a local PMTiles file** | 1️⃣ Add the PMTiles loader script, 2️⃣ Register the source, 3️⃣ Point the style to `pmtiles://mytiles.pmtiles`. See the **PMTiles section** below. |

---

## 3️⃣ Using a **local PMTiles** file (offline test)

If you have a `.pmtiles` file (e.g. generated with **Planetiler**, **Tippecanoe**, or **martin**), you can serve it from the same origin (or via a static-file CDN) and avoid any external network request.

```html
<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';
  import { PMTiles } from 'https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/pmtiles@latest/dist/PMTiles.js';

  // Register the protocol handler
  const protocol = new PMTiles('my-tiles.pmtiles');   // <-- path to your file
  maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', protocol.getTile);

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        mytiles: {
          type: 'vector',
          url: 'pmtiles://my-tiles.pmtiles'   // <-- note the protocol
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'my-layer',
          type: 'fill',
          source: 'mytiles',
          'source-layer': 'my_layer_name',   // <-- whatever layer name is in the .pmtiles
          paint: { 'fill-color': '#88c', 'fill-opacity': 0.5 }
        }
      ]
    },
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });
</script>
```

*Why this is handy*:  
- No API key, no rate-limit, no internet (once the file is on disk).  
- You can spin up a tiny **GitHub Pages** or **Vercel** site that just serves the `.pmtiles` file and the HTML above – perfect for CI or a quick demo.

---

## 4️⃣ If you already have a **Mapbox-style JSON** you love

1. **Export it from Mapbox Studio** (download the JSON).  
2. Open the JSON in **Maputnik** (`https://maputnik.github.io/`) – it will flag any `source` objects that still point at `mapbox://` URLs.  
3. Replace each source with a URL that points at your new tile service. Typical replacements:

   ```json
   // Mapbox source (won’t work)
   "sources": {
     "mapbox": {
       "type": "vector",
       "url": "mapbox://mapbox.mapbox-streets-v8"
     }
   }

   // OpenFreeMap equivalent (vector tiles)
   "sources": {
     "openfreemap": {
       "type": "vector",
       "url": "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/tiles/streets/{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf"
     }
   }
   ```

   *If you’re using a raster tile service, change `"type": "raster"` and use the `tiles` array instead of `url`.*

4. **Update `sprite` and `glyphs` URLs** if they still point at `mapbox://sprites/...` or `mapbox://fonts/...`.  
   - For the demo style you can just drop them: `sprite: "https://demotiles.maplibre.org/sprite/sprite"` and `glyphs: "https://demotiles.maplibre.org/font/{fontstack}/{range}.pbf"`.

5. Save the edited JSON and point your MapLibre map at it:

   ```js
   const map = new maplibregl.Map({
     container: 'map',
     style: '/styles/my-open-style.json', // local or hosted somewhere
     center: [-122.42, 37.78],
     zoom: 12
   });
   ```

---

## 5️⃣ Quick sanity-check checklist

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **Package** | `npm i maplibre-gl` (or use the CDN) |
| **Import** | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` (v6+ ES-module) |
| **Namespace** | Replace every `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl` (including CSS class prefixes) |
| **Token** | Delete `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'` |
| **Style URL** | Use one of the key-less URLs above **or** a custom style JSON that references non-Mapbox sources |
| **Sprites / Glyphs** | Point at public URLs (MapLibre demo, OpenFreeMap, or your own) |
| **Plugins** | Verify each Mapbox plugin works with MapLibre or swap to a MapLibre-native fork |
| **Geocoding / Directions** | Switch to Nominatim, Photon, OSRM, OpenRouteService, etc. (outside the scope of the map-load test) |
| **Test** | Open the page, confirm the basemap appears, and that any custom layers/markers still render. Open the browser console – there should be **no 401/403** errors about `mapbox://` URLs. |

---

## 6️⃣ TL;DR – One-liner you can copy-paste

```js
import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';
import 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // <-- free, no token
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12,
  // optional: add any controls you already used
}).addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl());
```

Run that in a blank HTML file, and you’ll have a fully functional MapLibre map **without any API key**. From there you can swap the `style` URL to any of the alternatives (OpenFreeMap, your own PMTiles, a custom style JSON, etc.) and continue migrating the rest of your app.

---

### 🎯 What you gain

* **Zero-cost basemap** for development and early-stage testing.  
* **Full control** over the tile source – you can later self-host, switch providers, or move to PMTiles without touching the map code again.  
* **No hidden token leakage** – everything you see in the network tab is a public URL you chose.

### ⚠️ What you give up (for now)

* The convenience of “one-click” Mapbox Studio styles.  
* Built-in Mapbox APIs (geocoding, directions, etc.) – you’ll need to replace those separately.

---

**Happy mapping!** If you hit a specific error after swapping the style URL (e.g., missing sprites, glyphs, or source-layer mismatches), drop the error message here and I can walk you through the exact fix. 🚀
